## Context

Tracker for the monitoring redesign accepted by the author on 2026-10-31,
memo `conception/2026-10-31-monitoring-redesign.md` (PR #2067). The thesis: record online only what cannot be
reconstructed later, never refuse on a record, derive the rest from durable
raw transcripts when a question needs it; build an index only when two
consumers need it (memo § 5 lists every deferred piece and its trigger).

Children, one merge request each:

- 1380: no online refusal (widened: writer recorded at landing, capture warns)
- 1383: raw archive of every runtime's transcripts, holes closed; date-bound,
  land before 2026-12-07
- 1384: launch line from every headless launcher (`seat_clock.py`, `manuscript_review.py`)
- 1385: timeline on demand (Blocked-by 1383, 1384)

## Exit criteria

- [ ] 1380, 1383, 1384 and 1385 closed
- [ ] Integration review (roar step 8): one raid session of the week renders as
      a timeline with its seats, from the archive, and its landing printed no
      attribution `invalid`
- [ ] Memo § 5 still states each deferred item with its trigger
